Caddy v2.11.7 is Apache-2.0. Its unchanged LICENSE is retained beside this file.
The statically linked Go runtime is BSD-3-Clause, with its LICENSE and exact fork
revision under ../go/. Linked module releases, upstream go.sum checksums and
complete upstream licence/notice texts are in modules.txt and
../dependencies/NOTICES.txt. Dependencies retain their individual terms.

Original Pyxis recipe, manifest and staging helper are MPL-2.0. Changes to
upstream files and the narrow platform files retain their upstream project terms.

Local changes:
- Select Caddy's existing non-POSIX signal path; os.Interrupt graceful shutdown
  remains in the upstream common path. No Unix signals are invented.
- Logrus uses native console detection. gRPC uses portable disconnect labels.
- readline is a nonterminal/plain-input dependency profile: raw mode, password
  capture and suspension are unsupported, and resize callbacks are not delivered.
- Tailscale state permissions and certificate-transparency platform root loading
  return explicit unsupported errors. Provided CT roots retain the pure-Go
  verifier. Normal Go TLS uses the native pinned boot CA bundle.
- Move Smallstep's unchanged pure SSH signer wrapper outside the SSH-agent
  backend build constraint so its nosshagentkms exclusion compiles. The backend
  remains registered as unsupported; no SSH agent is started or emulated.

Build tags: nobbolt,nobadger,nomysql,nopgx,nosshagentkms. Local ACME server,
optional database/key-store modules, Tailscale and arbitrary registered modules
are not qualified merely because the stock module list includes them. The
first profile is foreground explicit-address HTTP, reverse proxy and supplied
certificate/key TLS, with admin, automatic HTTPS/ACME and HTTP/3 disabled by
configuration. No HTTP/3 compile-out flag exists. Background start/reload,
automatic trust installation, subprocess execution and persistent certificate
management are outside this delivery.
